  overview: [
    "On the web a button is 32, 40 or 48 tall (`small`, default, `large`) with the 10 px control corner, a 500-weight label at 13, 14 or 16 px, and an 8 px gap beside its icons. The call to action fills with the accent, `destructive` with the status red, both under a lit top edge; `secondary` is the quiet well with a boundary, `outline` the boundary alone, `ghost` and `link` bare (the link underlined). A filled button brightens and rises 1 px under the pointer over 150 ms and settles back when it leaves; the other looks take the well's wash at once. A press scales the button to 96% and darkens it, unless `steadyPress`. A disabled button fades to 40%; a loading one keeps its full look while its spinner runs. A disabled or loading button stays put, and Reduce Motion makes the lift instant. On Android the button is the 40 dp Material 3 stadium, in the same colours.",
    "Pass `ref` to access the interactive Pressable, including link buttons. Use `useRef<ComponentRef<typeof Button>>(null)` from React, or `useRef<View>(null)` with React Native's `View` type. Object and callback refs are supported and detach on unmount. Calling `ref.current?.focus()` or `.blur()` delegates to the host without activating the control. Browser focus is supported; native focus depends on the platform and React Native version, and is separate from accessibility focus.",
    "`softHover` dims a link to 85% on hover in place of the wash. Inverse actions use a translucent white hover wash over a branded surface.",
    "Utility icon actions use `icon` with `compactIcon` (28), `mediumIcon` (32), or `largeIcon` (34). `wideIcon` gives the compact box two extra pixels of horizontal room; `circle` rounds it fully. Pair with `ghost` for a plain surface, `outline` for a boundary, or `ghost inset` for a quiet fill. `steadyPress` keeps the resting look while pressed, and `count` carries a notification badge over the upper trailing corner. The button still owns its accessible name, hover wash, and native touch-target extension.",
    "Use `inlineLink link small` for an inline text action: an underlined 13-pixel label with no box, read as a link and washed on hover. The default size is 14 pixels; `large` is 16. `extraBold`, `foreground`, and `inverse` set its weight and ink. `external` opens `href` through the system browser on every platform, while keeping its browser link semantics.",
    "`plainLink` is a plain accent text action with no box and no underline, still read as a button: a panel's Reset, a table's show-all row. On the web it is a 500 13 px label in the accent text ink (12 px with `small`) that brightens to the foreground ink under the pointer; natively it is the platform's own tint-coloured text button. Among the bodies, `inlineLink` wins over `plainLink` when both are passed.",
    "`scopeTrigger ghost steadyPress` is a bare 32 px menu trigger with a 600-weight 14px label; `filterTrigger ghost steadyPress` the same with a muted 13px label. Both take the well's wash on hover. Supply the trailing chevron through `iconRight`, and announce the menu with `expanded` and `haspopup`.",
    "`identityAction` is a 28 px hairline pill around a leading avatar and its name; `referenceLink` an underlined monospace key in the link ink; `inlineIcon` an unboxed 22 px icon action; `themeChoice` a 32 px pill around the theme's colour disc, a `<Swatch tiny ring circle decorative>` passed through `iconLeft`, whose `selected` state is the accent edge with a soft accent halo. `pageLink` is a page header's link, a 34 px hairline box around a muted 13 px label (a page's section, its source); add `mono` when the label is a path, which sets it in the 400 12 px mono face. `jumpLink` is a page's jump to one of its sections, a 28 px hairline pill around a muted 500 12 px label. Both header links brighten their label to the full ink and take the `secondary` wash under the pointer.",
  ],
